  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "resonant_vault",
      "name": "The Resonant Vault",
      "class": "dungeon",
      "offset": [
        53.0,
        0.0,
        39.0
      ],
      "arrival": [
        53.0,
        0.05,
        39.0
      ],
      "spaces": [
        "resonant_vault.approach",
        "resonant_vault.gallery",
        "resonant_vault.archive",
        "resonant_vault.brazier",
        "resonant_vault.lens",
        "resonant_vault.hall",
        "resonant_vault.stairhead",
        "resonant_vault.archiveway",
        "resonant_vault.brazierway",
        "resonant_vault.lensway",
        "resonant_vault.crossing",
        "resonant_vault.hallway"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Dressed slate and brass throughout, against the ochre dust of the region above: the Glasswardens built down away from the storm.",
        "The gallery walkways are scenery, not walk surfaces. They are reachable from nowhere, and marking them walkable would let the grounding ray stand an actor two metres above the bench floor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "geode_hollow",
      "name": "The Geode Hollow",
      "class": "cave",
      "offset": [
        193.0,
        0.0,
        39.0
      ],
      "arrival": [
        193.0,
        0.05,
        39.0
      ],
      "spaces": [
        "geode_hollow.mouth",
        "geode_hollow.throat",
        "geode_hollow.hollow",
        "geode_hollow.mirror",
        "geode_hollow.descent",
        "geode_hollow.gullet",
        "geode_hollow.mirrorway"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "No dressed stone and no brass anywhere in this package. It is the one interior that is not built, only entered, and it earns its place by being unlike the other three.",
        "The crystal lining is placed on a radial falloff, so shards are dense against the walls and thin over the floor a player actually crosses."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "shardworks",
      "name": "The Shardworks",
      "class": "workings",
      "offset": [
        83.0,
        0.0,
        229.0
      ],
      "arrival": [
        83.0,
        0.05,
        229.0
      ],
      "spaces": [
        "shardworks.headframe",
        "shardworks.sorting",
        "shardworks.cutting",
        "shardworks.stope",
        "shardworks.deep",
        "shardworks.shaft",
        "shardworks.cuttingway",
        "shardworks.stopeway",
        "shardworks.winze"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "The headframe is open to the sky, so the shaft reads as a hole in the barrens rather than as a door in a wall.",
        "Warm timber and iron against cold crystal is the whole point: this is the only interior of the four where people are working."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "storm_barrow",
      "name": "The Storm Barrow",
      "class": "barrow",
      "offset": [
        218.0,
        0.0,
        229.0
      ],
      "arrival": [
        218.0,
        0.05,
        230.0
      ],
      "spaces": [
        "storm_barrow.dromos",
        "storm_barrow.antechamber",
        "storm_barrow.strikewell",
        "storm_barrow.cella",
        "storm_barrow.stair",
        "storm_barrow.wellway",
        "storm_barrow.cellaway"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "The strike well is the one space in these four interiors with no lid: it is open to the region's sky, and the storm is what is still using this room.",
        "Coarse rubble and unadorned ashlar only. Nothing here is Glasswarden work, and no brass appears until the Vault."
      ]
    }
  ],
